aint Andrew","sight",21.30972,-157.85722,"229 Queen Emma Square","","","","","r","Seat of the Episcopal Diocese of Hawaii. Commissioned by King Kamehameha IV and Queen Emma and completed by King Kamehameha V in 1867."],["Kawaiahao Church","sight",21.30472,-157.85917,"957 Punchbowl St","","","","","r","The Westminster Abbey of Hawaii, historic church of Hawaiian royalty, constructed between 1836 and 1842 from coral rock. King Lunalias tomb is on the grounds and there is a historic cemetery adjacent to the church."],["Cathedral of Our Lady of Peace","sight",21.31075,-157.85942,"1184 Bishop St","","","","","r","Seat of the Roman Catholic Diocese of Honolulu, the original structure dates to 1843."],["Hawaiian Mission Houses Historic Site and Archives","sight",21.3039,-157.8569,"553 S King St","Tue Fri 10:30AM-2:30PM, Sat 10:30AM-3PM","","","","r","Three restored houses, temporary exhibition gallery, and research library provide a unique glimpse into 19th-century Hawaiian life. The houses are only accessible by guided tour Tu F Sa at 11AM and 1PM, and Sa 3PM."],["Foster Botanical Garden","sight",21.31667,-157.85917,"180 North Vineyard Blvd","9AM-4PM","","","","r","A collection of rare and beautiful plants from the tropical regions of the world. Docent-led tours everyday at 10:30AM."],["Hawaii State Capitol Building","sight",21.3073,-157.8573,"415 S Beretania St","closed due to COVID","","","","r","Completed in 1969, the State Capitol has a modern, open-air design, with pillars reminiscent of palm tree trunks, and two conical structures symbolizing volcanoes containing the House and Senate chambers, all surrounded by a moat of…"],["`Iolani Palace","sight",21.30662,-157.85896,"364 S King St","Tue-Sat 9AM-4PM. Guided tours 9AM-11:15AM, audio tours 11:45AM-3:30PM","","","","r","Iolani Palace dates back to 1882 and was the official residence of the Hawaiian Kingdom's last two monarchs. As a result of careful restoration and continued preservation, today's visitors to this National Historic Landmark in downtown…"],["Honolulu Hale","sight",21.30465,-157.85722,"530 S King St","","","","","r","In the Hawaiian language, \"Honolulu Hale\" literally means \"Honolulu House\", a fitting name for Honolulu's city hall."],["Liliuokalani Botanical Garden","sight",21.3167,-157.85,"123 N Kuakini St","7AM-5PM","","","","r","A 7.5 acre public city park, portions of which were a garden that belonged to Queen Liliuokalani, the last reigning Monarch of Hawaii. This is the only one of the five botanical gardens that contain only plants native to Hawaii."],["Honolulu Museum of Art","sight",21.3041,-157.8486,"900 S Beretania St","Thu 10AM-6PM, Fri-Sat 10AM-9PM, Sun 10AM-6PM","","","","r","This museum, founded in 1927 by Anna Rice Cooke, encompasses 32 galleries surrounding six courtyard gardens and houses one of the largest collections of Asian art in the United States, with an impressive Western collection to boot,…"],["The National Memorial Cemetery of the Pacific","sight",21.3119,-157.8452,"2177 Puowaina Dr","","","","","r","Situated in the middle of Punchbowl, an extinct crater, this is the final resting place for over 38,000 personnel from WWII, the Korean War and Vietnam. A shrine also commemorates the missing-in-action. It's also the resting place of…"],["Bangkok Chef Nuuana","restaurant",21.317,-157.8551,"1627 Nuuanu Ave","","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Honolulu Museum of Art Cafe","restaurant",21.30384,-157.84864,"Honolulu Museum of Art, 900 South Beretania St","","","","","r","Situated in an indoor/outdoor setting, it's usually packed with locals. It's the place to go for imaginative salads and sandwiches at a reasonable price. The art isn't bad either."]]}